# Line endings are a correctness problem here, not a style one.
#
# The guards compare file contents byte for byte — a skill mirror against its canonical copy — and
# that is how they first broke on Windows: with core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, a file the
# framework generated in LF was compared with one git had checked out as CRLF, never matched, and
# `npm run guard` failed on a clean tree with nothing wrong. `npm run sync:agents` then wrote LF,
# git converted it back on the next checkout, and the failure returned for good
# (.agents/docs/DECISIONS.md #19).
#
# So: everything textual is LF in the working tree as well as in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, whatever the platform.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Lockfiles are generated; a diff of one is noise in review.
package-lock.json  linguist-generated=true -diff
